.TH OCR 1 "2026-03-12" "toolbox" "Toolbox Commands"

.SH NAME
ocr \- perform optical character recognition on an image

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocr
.RB [ \-l
.IR LANG ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR FILE ]
.IR IMAGE

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B ocr
command extracts text from an image using Tesseract OCR.

The input image can be any format supported by Tesseract
such as PNG, JPEG, or TIFF.

If no output file is specified, the recognized text is written to stdout.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-l LANG
Specify the OCR language (default: eng).

.TP
.B \-o FILE
Write OCR output to FILE instead of stdout.

.TP
.B \-h
Display help information.

.SH EXAMPLES

Extract text from an image:

.EX
ocr image.png
.EE

Extract Russian text:

.EX
ocr -l rus newspaper.png
.EE

Save output to file:

.EX
ocr -l rus -o result.txt page.png
.EE

.SH AUTHOR
Thiago Ribeiro

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tesseract (1)
